  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Pankaj Dattatray Turekar vs The State Of Maharashtra on 2 December, 2022 Author: Anuja Prabhudessai Bench: Anuja Prabhudessai P.H. Jayani 05 ABA3357.2022.doc In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction Anticipatory Bail Application No. 3357 Of 2022 Mr. Pankaj Dattatray Turekar .... Applicant v/s. The State of Maharashtra .... Respondent Mr. Shaikh Asif Ali i/b. M/s. A.A. Siddiquie and Associates for the Applicant. Ms. Rutuja Ambekar, App for the State. Coram: Smt. Anuja Prabhudessai, J. Dated : 02nd December, 2022. P. C. :- .",
    "facts": "The Applicant has filed this Application under section 438 of Cr.P.C. apprehending his arrest in C.R.No.1417/2022 registered with Hadapsar Police Station, Pune for offences punishable under sections 272, 273, 328 of the Indian Penal Code, 1860 and sections 26(2)(i), 26(2)(iv), 3(1)(zz)(iv) and section 59 of The Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. 2. The case of the prosecution is that a tempo bearing registration No.MH-12-RN-8865 which was carrying gutkha was intercepted. The contraband was seized and the driver was placed under arrest. It is stated that on the basis of the statement of the co-accused, the Applicant has been arrayed as an accused. The issue relating to the applicability of section 328 of the Indian Penal Code in such matters, is pending before the Hon'ble Supreme Court. Furthermore, as on date, the only material against the Applicant is the statement of the co-accused.",
